Resize a block only in place

C dlmalloc offers realloc_in_place, which grows or shrinks a block where
it stands and fails instead of moving it; this crate's realloc always
moves a block it cannot resize in place, copying it inside the call. An
allocator that guards the heap with a lock needs the in-place step on its
own, so that it can copy a moved block after releasing the lock.
c_realloc_in_place exposes it.

License: MIT OR Apache-2.0 (dlmalloc 0.2.14)

